"<h1>Study One: facilitator guide</h1>\n<p><strong>Help the same attendees answer a questionnaire before and after Big Brue, so we can see whether their approach to conflict, connection and understanding changes.</strong></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://experiments.evolvable.me/study-one\">Participant questionnaire</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"https://experiments.evolvable.me/study-one?preview=1\">Preview for organisers \u2014 no responses submitted</a></p>\n<h2>What are we trying to learn?</h2>\n<p>The hypothesis is that festival experiences may help people see conflict as more constructive, become more willing to engage with different views, and develop a broader understanding of an issue\u2014even when their position does not change. Study One also asks about felt connection and outlook.</p>\n<p>We compare each person\u2019s answers before and after the festival and ask what they experienced. This reveals reported changes and associations; it cannot establish that the festival caused them. <a href=\"https://www.notion.so/3d07d52ecd5481128df1c7210c427521\">Study overview</a>, <a href=\"https://www.notion.so/3d67d52ecd5481298f6dd11f36ee1d86\">discussion of the intended outcomes</a>.</p>\n<h2>What happens?</h2>\n<p><strong>Invitation \u2192 before questionnaire \u2192 attend normally \u2192 personal email link \u2192 after questionnaire \u2192 compare matched answers</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Before attending any festival activities:</strong> an attendee aged 18 or over reads the study information, chooses whether to participate and completes the first questionnaire. The published estimate is about eight minutes; allow a little breathing room.</li>\n<li><strong>After saving those answers:</strong> they may separately provide an email address and agree to receive the second questionnaire. This is optional. The optional Evolvable link at the end is also entirely separate from taking part.</li>\n<li><strong>During the festival:</strong> they attend normally. Study One requires no special briefing, assigned panel or facilitated conversation. The panel-briefing intervention belongs to Study Two.</li>\n<li><strong>After the festival:</strong> the research assistant emails each consenting participant their own link. It automatically matches the second questionnaire to the first\u2014no code to remember. Participants revisit the measures and selected topic/view, and report attendance and what, if anything, they understood differently.</li>\n<li><strong>The study team:</strong> compares matched answers, keeping the different outcomes separate and noting missing follow-ups.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Who does what?</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<tr><td>Actor</td><td>Action</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Richard and Beau</td><td>Complete the handover to organisers and settle outstanding delivery arrangements. The recorded handover is Richard \u2192 Beau \u2192 organisers; organiser acceptance is not established by the website being live.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Festival organisers</td><td>Agree the invitation channel and timing, distribute the participant link, and make time for completion before activities begin.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Attendees</td><td>Decide freely, answer for themselves, attend normally and\u2014if they opt in\u2014complete the personal follow-up.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Designated research assistant</td><td>Use the protected workspace to prepare and send permitted follow-ups, record delivery, and handle link problems and participant requests. A named person still needs to be confirmed.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Study team</td><td>Review matched results and manage access and data handling.</td></tr>\n</table></div>\n<p>The <a href=\"https://www.notion.so/3ca7d52ecd54811884c5ca46ce2dfddb\">Brufest workstream</a> records the handover and manual email responsibilities.</p>\n<h2>Organiser checklist</h2>\n<p><strong>Before invitations go out</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confirm who distributes the invitation, who sends follow-ups and who monitors replies. The current study contact is <strong>beau@labofmisfits.com</strong>; confirm authorised sending access and inbox cover.</li>\n<li>Share the participant link above through the agreed festival channel. If using a QR code, point it to that link. Use the preview link only for rehearsal.</li>\n<li>Schedule completion before attendees encounter festival activities. The current implementation closes the first questionnaire at <strong>10:00 BST on Saturday 19 September 2026</strong> and opens the second at <strong>00:00 BST on Monday 21 September 2026</strong>. Confirm these configured times fit the invitation plan, including Sunday-only attendees.</li>\n<li>Rehearse on a phone in preview mode; check connectivity and the programme choices. Do not enter practice answers into the live study.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>When helping attendees</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Explain the two questionnaires and optional email choice. Let people read the information and consent themselves.</li>\n<li>Help with navigation, without suggesting answers or telling people they should become more open-minded. People can skip questions or stop.</li>\n<li>Remind those opting in to check their email address and keep their personal link private.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>After the festival</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The research assistant opens the <a href=\"/administration/study-one\">protected assistant workspace</a>, checks the saved first response and email permission, and copies the correct personal follow-up draft into the agreed email system. Exclude demonstration records.</li>\n<li>Send each link only to its saved recipient. Record it as sent externally only after sending; record failures separately. <strong>The website does not send emails.</strong></li>\n<li>For a lost link, check the request and resend to the saved address. Direct withdrawal or other participant requests to the study contact. Keep contact lists and personal links private.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Source and status note</h2>\n<p>Prepared <strong>10 September 2026</strong> from live Notion overview/workstream reads, the linked 8\u20139 September meeting summaries, the completed Study One implementation task and its source, and the current public preview. The preview shows the latest destructive-to-generative conflict item; existing participants retain their matched questionnaire version.</p>\n<p>The questionnaires, optional contact consent, personal matching links and protected assistant workflow are implemented. Invitation distribution, named staffing, inbox access and practical timing still require real-world confirmation. Older design pages include an additional delayed follow-up; this guide describes the implemented two-questionnaire flow. The guide creates no new study procedure or questionnaire change.</p>"